WEBVTT

00:12.250 --> 00:14.080
Noel Stollen...

00:14.352 --> 00:15.296
Found you.

01:46.734 --> 01:50.704
I'm telling you. Nobody's coming.

01:51.088 --> 01:53.440
Quiet. I can't interview like this.

01:53.648 --> 01:59.984
Any Seeker at a level high enough to come here
would already be in a party or clan.

02:00.384 --> 02:04.406
This is none of your business, Wolf. Get lost.

02:05.046 --> 02:09.376
Don't be like that.
Talkers can't fight alone, right?

02:09.616 --> 02:12.224
Join my party. We'd love to have you.

02:13.664 --> 02:14.960
Lightning Bite.

02:15.872 --> 02:19.664
With Wolf the Swordsman as leader
and Lycia the elf Archer,

02:19.664 --> 02:25.744
on top of other skilled members,
hopes are high for this C-Rank rookie party.

02:26.160 --> 02:31.888
You'd be guaranteed to make money if you join us,
unlike if you look for new members.

02:33.107 --> 02:36.320
- I'm telling you...
- That's enough, Wolf.

02:37.104 --> 02:38.816
You're bothering Noel.

02:39.068 --> 02:42.928
This is why the girl from
the flower shop turned you down.

02:44.624 --> 02:48.912
Wha... Lycia! That was private!
You can't just tell everyone!

02:48.912 --> 02:52.373
And you haven't even seen
my real negotiation skill yet!

02:52.464 --> 02:52.928
Wolf.

02:53.808 --> 02:55.370
Interested now?

02:55.488 --> 02:58.160
Yeah, on one condition.

02:59.456 --> 03:04.440
- You hear that? If it's a guy, I can...
- If I'm the leader.

03:05.504 --> 03:06.064
Huh?

03:06.816 --> 03:08.112
That's okay. Isn't it?

03:08.704 --> 03:09.984
I don't mind.

03:09.984 --> 03:10.960
Nor do I.

03:11.279 --> 03:12.544
Fine with me!

03:12.720 --> 03:16.693
Huh?! You all agree right away?
Don't I get input?!

03:16.768 --> 03:19.568
Noel is smarter than you. Is there some issue?

03:19.808 --> 03:22.032
I guess that's true...

03:22.256 --> 03:25.824
Wait, wait, there are tons of issues!

03:25.824 --> 03:29.248
I'm the leader! I founded Lightning Bite!

03:30.599 --> 03:32.752
Are you Noel Stollen?

03:34.656 --> 03:36.496
No way! Since when?!

03:36.704 --> 03:37.712
This girl...

03:38.352 --> 03:41.584
Lycia is very perceptive,
and she didn't notice her.

03:42.064 --> 03:43.776
I'm Alma.

03:44.096 --> 03:46.768
I saw your bulletin in the square.

03:53.792 --> 03:57.328
How old are you? You know minors can't be Seekers.

03:57.872 --> 04:00.800
Twenty-one. A grown adult.

04:01.072 --> 04:03.504
Five years older than Noel?!

04:03.842 --> 04:05.152
Favorite food?

04:05.232 --> 04:05.968
Strawberries.

04:06.256 --> 04:07.152
Hobby?

04:07.224 --> 04:07.974
Taking walks.

04:08.047 --> 04:09.857
Pastime?

04:09.968 --> 04:11.240
Stretching.

04:11.328 --> 04:12.834
Favorite book?

04:12.912 --> 04:18.096
Elizabeth Grese, "100 Techniques
for a Girl Who Wants to Be a Tough Guy."

04:18.528 --> 04:19.856
Job and rank?

04:20.576 --> 04:22.656
Scout. C-Rank.

04:23.296 --> 04:25.888
A Scout. Not bad.

04:26.432 --> 04:31.616
It's good to have an Archer or Scout
who can detect danger when exploring Abysses.

04:32.400 --> 04:34.912
It's a shame she didn't show up earlier.

04:35.648 --> 04:37.360
Final question.

04:37.760 --> 04:39.744
Why do you want to be a Seeker?

04:40.144 --> 04:42.144
I'm not interested in being a Seeker.

04:42.544 --> 04:44.464
What I'm interested in...

04:44.848 --> 04:47.808
is you, the grandson of Overdeath.

04:48.336 --> 04:49.952
You know my grandfather?

04:50.416 --> 04:51.408
I don't.

04:51.888 --> 04:54.848
But my grandpa once fought him.

04:55.264 --> 04:58.064
He lost his right arm.

04:59.344 --> 05:03.008
Don't tell me you've come to avenge him.

05:03.104 --> 05:06.576
No. That wouldn't be productive.

05:07.184 --> 05:12.080
I just wanted to know
what kind of Seeker that hero's grandson is.

05:12.688 --> 05:13.488
Is that so?

05:14.232 --> 05:17.168
Sorry. My grandfather has already passed.

05:17.520 --> 05:20.976
You'll have to accept my apology in his place.

05:21.152 --> 05:22.982
My grandpa died last month too.

05:23.072 --> 05:25.280
The past is in the past. No apology needed.

05:25.904 --> 05:27.920
What was his name?

05:28.848 --> 05:30.688
Alcor Judikhali.

05:34.873 --> 05:37.808
Alcor Judikhali...

05:38.545 --> 05:39.982
The Society of Assassins.

05:40.396 --> 05:44.620
A secret society that will
take out anyone you want if you can afford it.

05:45.776 --> 05:49.136
Alcor is its head and founder.

05:50.256 --> 05:51.824
He's a legendary assassin.

05:53.248 --> 05:56.000
You're Alcor's granddaughter?

05:56.448 --> 05:58.864
That's not a funny joke.

05:59.104 --> 06:03.936
You think we buy that nonsense?

06:04.300 --> 06:06.240
This doesn't concern you, Logan.

06:06.295 --> 06:09.943
There are unwritten rules in Seeker bars.

06:10.368 --> 06:14.160
You gotta go to the right bar for your rank.

06:14.265 --> 06:15.433
News to me.

06:15.680 --> 06:17.776
Just like I thought. You're a rookie.

06:18.936 --> 06:27.105
For your information, whoever breaks that rule
gets beaten up by the regulars. It's a custom.

06:27.207 --> 06:28.688
Noel. Question.

06:29.216 --> 06:29.792
What?

06:30.144 --> 06:32.576
What determines Seeker rank?

06:33.088 --> 06:34.544
Primarily your Job Rank.

06:35.088 --> 06:37.920
That and the capability you display.

06:38.064 --> 06:40.112
Okay. Understood.

06:40.480 --> 06:41.600
In that case...

06:41.984 --> 06:45.264
I just need to beat down
this self-righteous ape, right?

06:45.488 --> 06:46.672
Hey, now...

06:46.896 --> 06:50.096
That's the last thing you should say to Logan.

06:51.472 --> 06:53.248
Who're you calling an ape?!

06:53.248 --> 06:57.621
You're not going home alive, you pig!

06:59.088 --> 07:00.320
Too slow.

07:05.696 --> 07:07.056
Okay. All done.

07:13.712 --> 07:15.184
You're hired!

07:22.016 --> 07:23.600
I'm hungry.

07:30.880 --> 07:32.240
This is delicious!

07:32.480 --> 07:36.160
It's a fried bun. They can't be that uncommon.

07:36.448 --> 07:39.312
They don't have good food
like this in the mountains!

07:40.512 --> 07:43.936
So you weren't lying about
being Alcor's granddaughter.

07:44.720 --> 07:47.040
You didn't believe me either?

07:47.152 --> 07:51.952
Well, you just showed up and claimed
to be related to a legendary assassin.

07:53.030 --> 07:55.616
But I believed you right away.

07:55.920 --> 07:58.224
That you're Overdeath's grandson.

08:00.016 --> 08:01.184
Your eyes.

08:01.934 --> 08:05.264
Eyes that say you'd do anything to win.

08:06.320 --> 08:10.624
My grandpa told me never to fight Overdeath.

08:10.973 --> 08:13.973
That he'd always do what you least expect.

08:14.080 --> 08:17.248
That you can't fight fair against him and win.

08:17.838 --> 08:21.248
Your eyes remind me of that advice.

08:22.947 --> 08:26.832
Have you been training
to be an assassin in the mountains?

08:27.158 --> 08:32.080
Yes. To go from a Scout to an Assassin and beyond.

08:32.832 --> 08:37.056
I haven't leveled up to B-Rank yet,
but I meet the conditions.

08:37.552 --> 08:43.104
Why haven't you joined
the Society of Assassins if you're that capable?

08:43.648 --> 08:45.568
I meant to.

08:49.504 --> 08:51.024
Are you ready?

08:53.504 --> 08:58.976
Disappointing. This weak-looking guy
is my exam opponent?

08:59.232 --> 09:02.512
What?! Don't get cocky, C-Ranker!

09:02.624 --> 09:05.376
I'll show you an assassin's power!

09:17.840 --> 09:20.032
Stop! This is an exam!

09:20.512 --> 09:24.357
My grandpa said only the strong survive here.

09:24.464 --> 09:27.536
The weak are sacrificed
to the god of the underworld.

09:27.888 --> 09:31.200
That was in the former generation of the Society!

09:31.248 --> 09:33.296
That outdated rule...

09:33.310 --> 09:36.304
I don't care. That's what I learned.

09:36.816 --> 09:37.824
That's enough.

09:40.288 --> 09:41.136
You are?

09:42.920 --> 09:44.592
Simon Gregory.

09:45.888 --> 09:47.808
The new head of the Society.

09:49.902 --> 09:51.872
But they didn't let me in.

09:52.400 --> 09:56.656
They said I wasn't good enough for the Society.

09:57.200 --> 09:58.720
Despite your skill?

09:58.994 --> 10:00.720
They approved of my skill.

10:01.120 --> 10:04.224
But they said I wasn't a good fit.

10:06.232 --> 10:10.064
They said they're renewing the organization,

10:10.256 --> 10:13.136
so they don't need old-style Assassins.

10:14.091 --> 10:18.224
The Society was an independent
underground group before.

10:18.288 --> 10:21.536
But they're planning to affiliate
with the crown soon.

10:22.512 --> 10:24.944
So they'll be an officially
recognized organization?

10:25.187 --> 10:26.096
Apparently.

10:26.720 --> 10:30.992
So they'll mainly do espionage
instead of contract killing.

10:31.248 --> 10:35.856
The new head said that
would be best for the Society.

10:37.552 --> 10:42.704
That's extremely sensitive information!
Not something you should talk about over a bun.

10:42.913 --> 10:46.096
Right, that was supposed to be a secret!

10:46.144 --> 10:46.944
What now?

10:48.002 --> 10:49.664
"What now?"

10:50.032 --> 10:54.448
Are they going to send
a bunch of assassins to shut me up?

10:54.656 --> 10:56.288
Don't worry, Noel.

10:57.792 --> 11:02.416
If anything happens,
your big sister will protect you. It'll be okay.

11:04.240 --> 11:05.872
Who made you my big sister?!

11:07.930 --> 11:10.928
[III - True Talent]

11:12.720 --> 11:16.872
How much do you know about buffers?

11:16.960 --> 11:19.104
Not much.

11:19.742 --> 11:24.763
Their combat skills are weak,
but they have powerful support skills.

11:24.864 --> 11:27.840
Their job is to use those
to buff their party members.

11:27.917 --> 11:28.944
That's right.

11:29.456 --> 11:32.768
But it's more than just using buffs.

11:33.216 --> 11:34.032
It is?

11:34.208 --> 11:37.296
Firstly, there are many types of buffs.

11:37.824 --> 11:42.416
For example, there's a Talker skill
called Assault Command.

11:42.768 --> 11:45.872
It's powerful enough to end a fight in one shot,

11:45.993 --> 11:48.891
but if you use it at the wrong time,
the party could be wiped.

11:49.024 --> 11:50.752
Scary.

11:51.040 --> 11:55.616
That's why buffers have to be
aware of the battlefield before using any skills.

11:56.440 --> 11:59.984
We give the orders that will
maximize our party's capabilities,

12:00.016 --> 12:02.976
and we observe and control the flow of the battle.

12:03.856 --> 12:05.776
That's a buffer's real job.

12:06.380 --> 12:09.856
But Talkers can't use buff skills on themselves.

12:10.112 --> 12:13.088
We're not meant to
be able to fight at all, really.

12:13.312 --> 12:16.064
But you can.

12:16.800 --> 12:18.960
I'd be long dead if I couldn't.

12:23.224 --> 12:26.320
I want you to capture a monster, Alma.

12:26.747 --> 12:27.952
A monster?

12:28.591 --> 12:32.048
A creature that's mutated
due to an Abyss's influence.

12:32.763 --> 12:35.376
They're not as dangerous
as beasts, but they're tough.

12:36.144 --> 12:39.024
Hunting them is one of a Seeker's jobs.

12:39.544 --> 12:40.736
A killer rabbit.

12:40.880 --> 12:43.392
A rabbit monster with an iron horn.

12:43.680 --> 12:46.208
Ooh, cute. Can I eat it?

12:46.704 --> 12:47.504
No.

12:48.160 --> 12:52.672
Don't let its looks deceive you.
These things are vicious.

12:53.232 --> 12:55.280
I want you to catch it as an experiment.

12:55.408 --> 12:56.304
An experiment?

12:57.200 --> 13:01.952
Catch it with one of my buffs active on you.

13:02.400 --> 13:05.968
Piece of cake. I don't need your help.

13:06.064 --> 13:10.656
But what do you think will happen
if I add a buff on top of your existing skill?

13:11.776 --> 13:14.768
What's easy for me will be even easier?

13:14.815 --> 13:16.144
You'd think so, right?

13:16.768 --> 13:18.704
But it's not that simple.

13:19.255 --> 13:25.600
It depends on the individual whether
you can utilize your buffed skills effectively.

13:26.704 --> 13:29.232
Scouts have a skill called Accel, right?

13:29.427 --> 13:32.432
Yes. It doubles your speed.

13:32.779 --> 13:35.888
It can be stacked. I can use up to five.

13:37.029 --> 13:39.136
Could you do that from the start?

13:39.590 --> 13:43.680
No. I had to practice to get used to the speed.

13:43.872 --> 13:47.344
Otherwise I would tear muscles or break bones.

13:47.824 --> 13:50.864
Exactly. That's the case even for your own skills.

13:51.344 --> 13:56.768
To take advantage of buffs,
you have to train to adapt to them.

13:56.848 --> 13:57.888
I see.

13:58.464 --> 14:01.792
This experiment will test your adaptability.

14:02.272 --> 14:06.320
The results will determine
what we do going forward.

14:07.712 --> 14:12.160
My former members were talented,
and even they needed half a month to adapt.

14:12.640 --> 14:13.456
You should...

14:13.456 --> 14:16.112
Don't worry. I'll get results.

14:19.152 --> 14:21.952
How many killer rabbits are there in the area?

14:22.736 --> 14:25.888
Thirteen within two hundred meters.

14:26.279 --> 14:27.328
That's plenty.

14:27.840 --> 14:29.344
Commence the experiment!

14:29.760 --> 14:31.936
Battle Voice! Tactician!

14:33.136 --> 14:34.272
How do you feel?

14:35.088 --> 14:40.192
Strange. I can feel power
welling up from deep inside.

14:40.880 --> 14:43.536
As long as you follow my orders,

14:43.840 --> 14:45.968
all your stats will be boosted.

14:46.176 --> 14:47.280
Amazing...

14:48.083 --> 14:50.656
Use as many Accels as you can.

14:51.040 --> 14:54.368
A stack of five should have
the effect of six or more.

14:54.816 --> 14:55.568
Got it.

14:56.928 --> 15:01.424
Catch at least one killer rabbit
within ten seconds and you pass.

15:02.160 --> 15:05.312
Order! Catch a killer rabbit!

15:05.792 --> 15:06.528
Accel.

15:08.720 --> 15:09.728
Quintuple!

15:17.808 --> 15:18.672
Amazing.

15:18.928 --> 15:20.768
I feel light as a feather.

15:22.752 --> 15:25.696
So this is what a Talker can do!

15:26.624 --> 15:29.536
Five. Six. Seven.

15:29.872 --> 15:30.832
I'm back!

15:31.792 --> 15:35.200
Thirteen in all. They're unconscious.

15:35.824 --> 15:37.552
You caught them all?!

15:37.904 --> 15:39.920
Yes. How long was that?

15:40.704 --> 15:42.128
8.6 seconds.

15:43.046 --> 15:46.464
To think you'd utilize
your first buff so effectively.

15:47.328 --> 15:49.616
That's inborn talent for you.

15:50.672 --> 15:51.776
I'm jealous.

15:53.056 --> 15:54.896
Is the experiment still going?

15:55.225 --> 15:57.040
No, that was enough.

15:57.360 --> 15:59.984
Judging by that, you don't even need training.

16:02.107 --> 16:03.040
On that note...

16:03.584 --> 16:06.672
I think it's time to take a job as a party.

16:06.992 --> 16:11.008
Ooh, our first job. I've never explored an Abyss.

16:12.128 --> 16:12.864
A letter?

16:13.184 --> 16:17.088
Yeah. I took a job from a village
I hunted monsters in before.

16:17.414 --> 16:20.112
"Dear Noel Stollen,"

16:20.256 --> 16:24.352
"A band of thieves has come to
the outskirts of Mintz Village."

16:26.352 --> 16:30.336
The new Blue Beyond's first job
is hunting thieves.

16:32.864 --> 16:35.472
This is my first time on a stagecoach.

16:35.856 --> 16:37.104
This is fun!

16:37.648 --> 16:39.632
It's only fun at first.

16:40.160 --> 16:43.168
It's a long, boring commute to Mintz Village.

16:43.520 --> 16:44.864
It's that far?

16:45.136 --> 16:48.128
Yeah. Your bottom will get stiff as a rock.

16:49.056 --> 16:53.472
I'll tell you about Seeker work to pass the time.

16:55.424 --> 16:56.096
Please do.

16:57.712 --> 17:01.472
Seekers do a wide variety of jobs.

17:01.824 --> 17:04.608
It's not just hunting beasts
that spawn in Abysses.

17:05.552 --> 17:07.984
There are Monster Hunts,
where we take down monsters.

17:08.912 --> 17:12.032
Crime Hunts, where we track down
and capture criminals.

17:12.944 --> 17:16.000
And Treasure Hunts,
where we search for valuable items.

17:16.768 --> 17:20.128
There are even Mythic Hunts
where we explore mystic lands.

17:20.800 --> 17:26.400
Gangs of thieves like the one we're dealing with
would normally be the lord's problem.

17:27.484 --> 17:29.424
But they're slow to act.

17:30.112 --> 17:32.896
The village would be dust by the time help came.

17:33.712 --> 17:37.520
That's why we Seekers get these requests.

17:37.728 --> 17:38.896
That's tough work.

17:39.279 --> 17:42.272
Yeah. Our clients are poor villagers.

17:42.771 --> 17:46.528
I don't expect much reward,
but this is perfect to test your chops.

17:46.950 --> 17:51.776
We'll take down the bad guys
bothering the nice villagers! I like it.

17:53.232 --> 17:55.296
I'm glad you feel that way.

18:16.288 --> 18:19.630
My butt is so sore... I hate carriages...

18:19.728 --> 18:23.136
I told you it's only fun at first.

18:23.920 --> 18:25.552
You meanie.

18:25.990 --> 18:28.928
We'll stay here in Eudora overnight.

18:29.333 --> 18:32.800
We'll get on another carriage
to Mintz Village tomorrow.

18:34.592 --> 18:39.344
I'm sorry. We're full tonight.

18:39.984 --> 18:42.016
Oh, well. Let's look elsewhere.

18:42.352 --> 18:43.904
We just ran out!

18:44.496 --> 18:45.840
Next inn!

18:46.032 --> 18:47.808
If you'd been a minute earlier...

18:47.936 --> 18:48.800
Next!

18:49.152 --> 18:50.272
We just had a room...

18:56.496 --> 18:57.712
Finally, we can rest.

18:58.240 --> 19:01.248
The food was awful, but I like the room.

19:01.584 --> 19:05.088
They only had a single room,
so you can use the bed.

19:05.696 --> 19:06.912
What about you?

19:07.184 --> 19:08.592
I'll sleep on the floor.

19:09.056 --> 19:11.920
Why? You could sleep with me.

19:12.080 --> 19:15.056
No... That wouldn't be a good idea.

19:15.504 --> 19:17.776
You're embarrassed. Cute.

19:17.808 --> 19:19.296
It's not that I'm embarrassed.

19:19.664 --> 19:21.232
Then let's sleep together!

19:21.232 --> 19:24.482
I'm your big sister Alma, Noel!
It's perfectly fine!

19:24.560 --> 19:26.144
Since when are you my big sister?!

19:30.992 --> 19:32.768
So cute.

19:47.504 --> 19:48.080
What?

19:49.755 --> 19:51.472
You're very fit.

19:52.754 --> 19:54.672
Wonderful. Great.

19:55.152 --> 19:57.216
Like an untamed beast.

19:57.872 --> 20:00.016
Perfect muscles with no excess.

20:00.432 --> 20:00.944
Hey.

20:02.427 --> 20:04.672
You have such a nice body.

20:05.271 --> 20:07.632
It's... unfortunate.

20:08.112 --> 20:08.960
Unfortunate?

20:10.368 --> 20:14.450
That you have to put in effort for that body.

20:14.654 --> 20:19.776
And no matter how hard you train,
you'll never be as good as a front-line Job.

20:20.794 --> 20:24.384
Hard work can never catch up to inborn talent.

20:25.088 --> 20:30.423
That's what's too bad. If you were
a Warrior like Overdeath,

20:30.572 --> 20:32.816
you could have been the ultimate Seeker.

20:35.216 --> 20:35.728
Alma.

20:36.384 --> 20:36.960
What?

20:37.296 --> 20:38.320
Close your eyes.

20:38.832 --> 20:39.632
Like this?

20:41.872 --> 20:42.680
Ow!

20:42.928 --> 20:43.920
What was that for?

20:44.160 --> 20:46.288
For the unnecessary comments.

20:46.808 --> 20:48.304
Go take a bath.

20:48.784 --> 20:49.840
I'm going to bed.

20:51.120 --> 20:51.920
Fine.

21:04.688 --> 21:08.832
You have to put in effort for that body.

21:09.005 --> 21:14.048
And no matter how hard you train,
you'll never be as good as a front-line Job.

21:14.505 --> 21:18.048
Hard work can never catch up to inborn talent.

21:19.411 --> 21:23.232
I know that better than anyone.

21:25.392 --> 21:26.755
Don't cry, Noel!

21:26.896 --> 21:29.968
But they said it's the weakest Job.

21:30.064 --> 21:33.616
I wanted to be a Warrior like you.

21:35.136 --> 21:39.216
Noel, you look just like your late mother.

21:39.824 --> 21:41.152
But I can tell.

21:42.177 --> 21:47.024
You have dormant talent as a Seeker just like me.

21:47.712 --> 21:49.920
No matter what you are, even a Talker,

21:50.064 --> 21:53.328
I'll make a great Seeker out of you.

21:54.176 --> 21:55.600
Trust me.

22:01.904 --> 22:02.848
